{
  "wasim_version": "0.1.0",
  "source": {
    "generator": null,
    "notes": "Digital (binary) options priced by exact-terminal Monte Carlo (one N(0,1) draw per realization, no discretization bias). Cash-or-nothing call = disc*1{S(T)>K} (closed form disc*N(d2)), asset-or-nothing call = disc*S(T)*1{S(T)>K} (S0*N(d1)), and a cash-or-nothing put with the exact per-path parity cash_call+cash_put=disc. The payoff is intentionally DISCONTINUOUS: the price is a smooth integral (MC converges fine), but its Greeks are not (pathwise fails, bump is noisy, likelihood-ratio is clean) - see DIGITAL_OPTION_SCOPE.md for the sensitivities gap this motivates. See DIGITAL_OPTION_EXAMPLE.md."
  },
